{"key":"59af8623398bb064","source_file":"Potts Sh - So.json","source_id":36918,"source_url":"concordance-snuffers-ppl-emunctoria","term":"Snuffers","headwords":["Snuffers","Snuffed"],"latin":["Emunctoria","Emunctus"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Snuffers"],"latin":["Emunctoria"]},{"english":["Snuffed"],"latin":["Emunctus"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","CL","SE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9572","subsection":null},"text":"Tongs and snuff-dishes are things to snuff with, thus things purificatory and evacuatory. The reason these are in the Natural, is that the Natural is the emunctory, thus the Purificatory and Evacuatory. Explained.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"CL","section":"380","subsection":"4"},"text":"As the candle had not been snuffed, it gave little light.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"3124","subsection":null},"text":"(The emunctories of the body.) DLove 5:2.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"snuffers","url":"/meta/potts/snuffers/"}